    "md5": "a31cf31192bd7e5b1af2bed8e150b609",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2004,
    "chunk_text": "Institute of Directors to host Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026\n\nPriyan Fernando,\u00a0Rajiv Krishnan,\u00a0Prof. Deba Bardhan Correia,\u00a0Himanshu Priyadarshi,\u00a0Duleesha Kulasooriya,\u00a0Prof. Harin Sellahewa,\u00a0Mohamed Nasheed\n\nExceptional international and Sri Lankan leaders to examine how boards must move from compliance to sustainable growth\n\nThe Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLID) will host Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026, on July 22, 2026, at Cinnamon Grand Colombo, under the theme \u2018Future-Ready Sri Lankan Directors \u2013 From Compliance to Sustainable Growth\u2019.\n\nRecognised as Sri Lanka\u2019s premier boardroom leadership event, the summit will bring together an exceptional line-up of internationally renowned business leaders, governance experts, academics and leading Sri Lankan directors to address one defining question: Are today\u2019s boards equipped not merely to govern organisations but to lead them confidently into an increasingly uncertain future?\n\nHeadlining the summit is former Maldives President and Speaker Mohamed Nasheed, who will share his perspectives on sustainability, resilience and the growing importance of environmental, social and governance considerations in shaping long-term corporate success.\n\nJoining him is internationally respected entrepreneur and Regent Global Group Chairman Prof. Selva Pankaj, who will explore how boards can lead innovation while balancing governance, risk and sustainable growth.\n\nInnovation and emerging technologies will be a key focus with Asia Pacific Innovation Leader and Deloitte\u2019s Centre for the Edge Managing Director Duleesha Kulasooriya.\n\nProviding further insight into technology governance is Professor of Computing and University of Buckingham Computing, Law and Psychology Faculty Dean Prof. Harin Sellahewa. His session will examine why directors must understand the strategic, legal and ethical implications of artificial intelligence (AI) and cybersecurity as these issues become central to board oversight."
